original_abstract='Let F=ℚ₃ and let E/F be its unramified quadratic extension. We give an explicit checkable argument that the Langlands quotient with segments [4,6],[2,5],[3,3],[1,4],[0,2] is Galois invariant, is not an entire proper parabolic induction, and has no invariant linear form for any Hermitian stabilizer in GL₁₅(E). The analytic proof assembles the period bases and functional equations of Feigon–Lapid–Offen: two invertible nested-segment swaps expose five necessary opposite-lift conditions forming an odd cycle. Noninduction follows from the Lapid–Mínguez ladder-side matching criterion, with all fifteen partition obstructions displayed. The total multiplicity is zero rather than the two predicted by the historical k=1 multiplicity conjecture. Historical priority and overlap with Luo–Zha, DOI 10.1007/s11464-025-0256-0, remain UNKNOWN: their complete paper was unavailable for comparison. No firstness or worldwide novelty claim is made.'
